
 # ------------------------------------------------------------------
 # BEGIN network-fault-diagnosis arrows (LEADSTO)
 # ------------------------------------------------------------------
 #
 # Fault propagation is a process, which is why it belongs in LEADSTO.
 # The base config already carries (cause), (aff), (result) and
 # (is prereq); those are reused rather than redefined here.
 #
 # Note the direction convention. Arrows are written cause to symptom,
 # so diagnosis walks them BACKWARDS. The inverse readings are therefore
 # the ones a diagnostic query actually uses, and they are worded to be
 # read aloud in that direction.

 :: fault propagation ::

  + manifests as the symptom    (manifests)    - is a symptom produced by      (symptom-of)
  + propagates to               (propagates)   - receives the fault from       (propag-from)
  + degrades into               (degrades)     - degraded from                 (degraded-from)

 :: triage, narrowing a vague complaint ::

  # A complaint is not a symptom. "The network is slow" is a report of
  # experience that has to be narrowed before the causal model can touch
  # it. Narrowing is a process, so it lives in LEADSTO.

  + is refined by asking        (refined-by)   - refines the complaint         (refines)
  + narrows to                  (narrows-to)   - is a narrowing of             (narrowed-from)

 :: playbook coverage as negative evidence ::

  # A playbook exists because the problem was already characterizable and
  # already has remediation. So a playbook that covers a fault and did NOT
  # fire is evidence against that fault, and a fault no playbook covers is
  # a prime suspect whenever a complaint arrives unexplained.

  + is detected by playbook     (detected-by)  - detects the fault             (detects)

 :: masking, why an expected symptom is absent ::

  # Masking is the thing that makes network faults hard. A cause can be
  # present and its usual symptom invisible, because something upstream
  # absorbed it. A diagnostic graph that cannot say this will quietly
  # rule out the right answer.

  + is masked by                (masked-by)    - masks the symptom of          (masks)

 :: discrimination, the part that narrows a hypothesis set ::

  + is discriminated by         (discrim-by)   - discriminates between causes  (discriminates)
  + is confirmed by observing   (confirmed-by) - would confirm                 (confirms)
  + is excluded by observing    (excluded-by)  - would exclude                 (excludes)

 :: remediation ::

  + is mitigated by             (mitig-by)     - mitigates                     (mitigates)
  + is resolved by              (resolved-by)  - resolves                      (resolves)

 # ------------------------------------------------------------------
 # END network-fault-diagnosis arrows (LEADSTO)
 # ------------------------------------------------------------------
